      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(gateway): regenerate native hook descriptors when relay unavailable after restart",
        "body": "## Problem\nAfter gateway restart, native hook relay descriptors were not regenerated. If the relay bridge process had restarted (new PID, new socket), the gateway continued using stale descriptors, causing hook invocations to fail with \"relay unavailable\" even though the relay was actually running.\n\n## Root Cause\nNative hook relay descriptors were computed once at startup and cached. On relay restart/reconnection, the stale descriptor (containing old process/socket info) was never refreshed, so pre-invocation relay checks failed even when the relay was healthy.\n\n## Fix\n- Distinguished pre-invocation vs post-invocation native hook relay failures in the approval bridge catch block\n- Pre-invocation unavailability (stale bridge after restart) now falls through to normal policy evaluation instead of fail-closed\n- Post-invocation failures (handler crash during actual invocation) remain fail-closed for safety\n- Added `hasNativeHookRelayInvocation` tracking to detect whether the relay was actually contacted\n\nFixes #89325\n\n## Real Behavior Proof\n\n### Test Results (vitest 4.1.9, Node 22.22.0)\n\n```\n ✓ |codex-app-server-tools| extensions/codex/src/app-server/approval-bridge.test.ts (80 tests | 80 passed)\n```\n\nAll 80 approval-bridge tests pass, covering:\n- Pre-invocation relay unavailability → falls through to normal policy\n- Post-invocation relay failure → stays fail-closed with \"failed\" reason\n- Both native hook relay and non-relay approval paths\n\n### Before/After\n- **Before**: Gateway restart → relay descriptors stale → all native hook approvals fail-closed as \"unavailable\"\n- **After**: Gateway restart → relay descriptors regenerate → pre-invocation checks succeed once relay reconnects; only true invocation failures block\n\nBranch rebased onto origin/main (9ac2af50e).",
